1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,382
I think this is ready.

2
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:11,970
See if the dough's burnt.

3
00:00:12,053 --> 00:00:13,054
Hey, it's…

4
00:00:14,139 --> 00:00:17,517
SMOKE BILLOWING

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,394
It's become crispy like a chip.

6
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,730
Let's just…

7
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:23,606
A BLACK CHIP?

8
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:25,150
Let's just…

9
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:28,528
Let's scrape it off.

10
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:30,238
Then, it'll be all right.

11
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:33,825
If we scrape it off
until we see the lighter part…

12
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,871
It's just like brick oven pizza, isn't it?

13
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:39,748
Brick oven, my foot.

14
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:40,790
Let's scrape it off.

15
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:46,629
Geez, he's actually scraping it.

16
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:51,551
Hey, it looks okay when you scrape it.

17
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:57,640
Damn it.

18
00:00:58,725 --> 00:00:59,851
Damn it.

19
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,855
PUTS TOPPINGS BACK

20
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:10,236
I have no choice.
I need to flip and scrape it.

21
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:17,994
What's that sound?

22
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:19,537
What? No, it's nothing.

23
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:21,706
It's going well.

24
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:25,126
Is there a problem?

25
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:26,044
No.

26
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:26,961
DENYING AGAIN

27
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:28,421
All right.

28
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:30,465
He's desperately denying any problems.

29
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:31,883
It's going well.

30
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:35,553
- Actually, things went as planned.
- Is that so?

31
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:37,597
Burning it was part of my plan.

32
00:01:38,431 --> 00:01:39,516
I expected it to happen.

33
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,644
- That's a relief then.
- Yeah.

34
00:01:42,727 --> 00:01:45,855
After this, if we reheat it
before serving it,

35
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:47,565
that will be the cherry on top.

36
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:50,652
- It worked like a charm.
- This is so funny.

37
00:01:50,735 --> 00:01:52,111
No one will notice.

38
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:00,662
This… Goodness.

39
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:03,623
PUTS TOPPINGS BACK AGAIN

40
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,045
I got rid of all the burnt parts though.

41
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:10,713
ALSO

42
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:14,134
HE ADDS MORE CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPERS

43
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:15,593
Okay.

44
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:17,512
MEANWHILE, DOWNSTAIRS

45
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:20,306
THEY DECORATE THE SINK CABINET

46
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:34,863
DRAWING THE STAFF'S CHARACTERS

47
00:02:34,946 --> 00:02:36,823
KIAN, YEON-KOUNG
ZUHA, JUN-HO

48
00:02:36,906 --> 00:02:39,075
- It's much better.
- Yeah.

49
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:41,327
- The vibe's a bit more…
- It's brightened up.

50
00:02:41,411 --> 00:02:43,288
This is the golden ratio.

51
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:45,915
THEY USE THE GOLDEN RATIO
TO MAKE THE WELCOME DRINKS

52
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:49,502
They'll like it.

53
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:51,254
Are they arriving soon?

54
00:02:51,337 --> 00:02:53,631
- Ya!
- Hoo!

55
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:55,258
WHAT'S THAT SOUND?

56
00:02:55,341 --> 00:02:57,135
- Someone's here.
- It must be the guys.

57
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:58,928
- Ya!
- Hoo!

58
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,096
Do they want us to open up?

59
00:03:00,179 --> 00:03:01,848
- To open the door for them?
- I think so.

60
00:03:06,227 --> 00:03:08,062
NEW GUESTS

61
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:11,149
Hello.

62
00:03:11,816 --> 00:03:14,027
- What is it?
- It's not them. They're new guests.

63
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:14,986
- New ones?
- Yes.

64
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:16,946
- Hello, nice to meet you.
- Hello.

65
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:19,240
- Try opening the door.
- How do we open it?

66
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:21,743
Open it any way you can.
Just give it a try.

67
00:03:21,826 --> 00:03:22,785
FLUSTERED

68
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:24,203
- But how?
- Any way you can.

69
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,830
I think they're father and son.

70
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:26,998
Really?

71
00:03:27,081 --> 00:03:28,917
It seems like a father and son are here.

72
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,627
Really? We should open it for them then.

73
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,712
We should give them the welcome drinks.

74
00:03:38,259 --> 00:03:39,093
It's open.

75
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:40,720
- Hello!
- Hello!

76
00:03:40,803 --> 00:03:41,804
Welcome.

77
00:03:41,888 --> 00:03:43,306
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

78
00:03:43,389 --> 00:03:44,599
- Hello, welcome.
- Hello.

79
00:03:44,682 --> 00:03:46,684
Hello. Welcome.

80
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:48,478
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

81
00:03:48,561 --> 00:03:49,687
- I'll carry it.
- No, let me.

82
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:51,064
All right. Thank you.

83
00:03:51,147 --> 00:03:53,274
- Welcome.
- Welcome.

84
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:55,360
First, here are your welcome drinks.

85
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:56,945
FIRST WELCOME DRINKS WITH NEW RECIPE

86
00:03:57,028 --> 00:03:58,154
- Hello.
- Take a sip first.

87
00:03:58,238 --> 00:03:59,739
GIVE IT A TRY

88
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:11,459
We mixed lemon juice with water.

89
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:13,127
Lemon juice?

90
00:04:13,211 --> 00:04:14,796
Thankfully, it's not mono maple sap.

91
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:16,881
Thank you. I like lemons.

92
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:19,092
- Please, come on in.
- Yes, come in.

93
00:04:22,553 --> 00:04:23,429
Hello.

94
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:24,639
- Hello.
- Hello.

95
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:27,058
Father and son?

96
00:04:27,141 --> 00:04:29,394
FATHER AND SON?

97
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:30,520
You're not his son?

98
00:04:30,603 --> 00:04:32,063
He's a senior colleague.

99
00:04:32,146 --> 00:04:33,564
I see!

100
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:36,567
We went to the same high school,
and we're from the same area.

101
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,570
He's my mentor.

102
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:41,239
I'm majoring in elementary education.

103
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,699
KIM SEONG-JUN

104
00:04:42,782 --> 00:04:44,659
I taught PE.
Now I'm an education supervisor.

105
00:04:44,742 --> 00:04:45,576
LEE SUNG-NAM

106
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:47,161
- Then, you're a public servant?
- Yes.

107
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:48,079
You too?

108
00:04:48,162 --> 00:04:50,081
I'm currently studying
as a college student.

109
00:04:50,164 --> 00:04:51,249
- College student?
- Yes.

110
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:52,292
KNOCKING

111
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:54,002
- Someone's here.
- Someone else is here.

112
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:58,256
Be careful.

113
00:04:58,339 --> 00:05:00,174
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

114
00:05:00,258 --> 00:05:01,718
- Did you have a good time?
- Hello.

115
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:03,219
- Yes.
- You look so cold.

116
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:04,804
THE KOREAN-JAPANESE COUPLE RETURNS

117
00:05:06,055 --> 00:05:08,057
Here are your welcome drinks.

118
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:09,058
Thank you.

119
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:12,103
I'm Japanese,
so you can talk to me in Japanese.

120
00:05:12,186 --> 00:05:13,980
Thank you.

121
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,443
- Explain to them, please.
- Yes.

122
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:20,028
He's the boss.

123
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:21,654
I'M THE BOSS

124
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:22,905
He's the boss.

125
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:25,825
JAPANESE MODE TURNS ON

126
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:29,829
No, I'll just speak Korean.

127
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:34,125
It's a studio apartment,
like a friend's place.

128
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:37,045
Like a friend's place,
it's a small studio apartment.

129
00:05:37,128 --> 00:05:38,004
I see.

130
00:05:38,087 --> 00:05:39,380
That's the concept,

131
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:41,841
and I wanted to make it
as big as possible.

132
00:05:41,924 --> 00:05:43,092
That's why it's huge.

133
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:46,262
WHEN THE BOSS TALKS, ZUHA TRANSLATES

134
00:05:46,345 --> 00:05:48,806
That's the kitchen and sink.

135
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:50,349
The kitchen's on the second floor.

136
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,977
There's also a fridge here and a TV there.

137
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:55,688
Usually, cooking oil and pots
are put in here, right?

138
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:57,940
OPENING THE SAUNA

139
00:05:58,024 --> 00:05:59,192
It's a sauna.

140
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:03,529
<i>I thought, "I never imagined this."</i>

141
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:06,532
<i>I thought it was something</i>
<i>only Kian84 could think of.</i>

142
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:08,534
5:00 P.M.

143
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:09,869
- That was fun.
- It was great.

144
00:06:09,952 --> 00:06:12,205
LUGE TEAM & JUN-HO ARE BACK

145
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:13,414
- They're back.
- They're back.

146
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:15,625
- Hey, speak of the devil.
- Seriously.

147
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:16,667
How was it?

148
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:18,669
- I was basically flying around. Yes.
- Really?

149
00:06:18,753 --> 00:06:21,047
Say hello. They're all new guests.

150
00:06:21,130 --> 00:06:22,673
- Hello.
- We have four new guests.

151
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,217
- Hello.
- Hello.

152
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,301
We came today.

153
00:06:25,384 --> 00:06:27,220
- Really? We came yesterday.
- Nice to meet you.

154
00:06:27,303 --> 00:06:29,097
Hello, it's nice to meet you.

155
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,265
ALL THE GUESTS ARE HERE

156
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:32,725
Are you hungry?

157
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:34,769
- Yes, totally.
- We haven't eaten anything today.

158
00:06:34,852 --> 00:06:38,523
The boss today is a bit…

159
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:39,857
Food for dinner…

160
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:41,234
He's preparing.

161
00:06:41,317 --> 00:06:42,360
- It's pizza.
- Pizza?

162
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:43,277
Yes, pizza.

163
00:06:43,861 --> 00:06:45,863
KIAN REHEATS THE PIZZAS

164
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:53,830
You know what? It looks good.

165
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:56,499
- It honestly does look delicious.
- Yeah.

166
00:06:58,126 --> 00:06:59,418
Let's eat!

167
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:01,963
I think the food is here.

168
00:07:02,046 --> 00:07:05,007
We can go get it over there.

169
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:07,468
Help me, please.

170
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:09,137
Please help me out.

171
00:07:09,762 --> 00:07:11,389
Take these and bring them over there.

172
00:07:11,472 --> 00:07:12,640
It's pizza!

173
00:07:12,723 --> 00:07:14,142
- It looks good.
- It's pizza.

174
00:07:15,351 --> 00:07:16,727
This will definitely be spicy.

175
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:17,937
You can't handle spicy food?

176
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:19,439
I am Japanese after all.

177
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:20,731
I'm not good with it either.

178
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:23,192
WORRIED IT MIGHT BE TOO SPICY

179
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:24,944
Gosh. Hey, Jun-ho.

180
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:27,238
- I'm really worried.
- I told you.

181
00:07:27,321 --> 00:07:30,032
GOING DOWN TO EAT
WHILE FULL OF WORRIES

182
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:31,701
Gosh, did you make it?

183
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:33,619
Kian did it all.

184
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:34,954
I DID

185
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:36,414
TOGETHER

186
00:07:38,249 --> 00:07:39,250
6:00 P.M.

187
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:41,919
We made pizza for dinner.

188
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:44,505
I made these darker ones.

189
00:07:44,589 --> 00:07:46,007
Kimchi pork belly pizzas.

190
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:49,218
And the lighter ones were made by Jun-ho.

191
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:51,053
We tried our best.

192
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:52,763
I hope you like it.

193
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:55,016
WORRIED

194
00:07:55,099 --> 00:07:57,059
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you.

195
00:07:57,143 --> 00:07:58,895
What? Was it hard to explain the food?

196
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,982
The ones I made are spicy,
and the lighter ones are not spicy.

197
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:18,706
HIS EYES ARE BUSY CHECKING THEIR REACTIONS

198
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,463
It's not bad, Boss.

199
00:08:25,546 --> 00:08:26,964
- It's not?
- No.

200
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:28,132
It tastes like real pizza.

201
00:08:28,216 --> 00:08:30,051
- Really?
- It's soft.

202
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:33,930
- It's not bad, Boss.
- It's not?

203
00:08:34,013 --> 00:08:36,265
It's amazing. The dough's good too.

204
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:37,850
Did you make the dough too?

205
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:39,268
- Yes.
- Yes.

206
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:41,229
He made everything himself.

207
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:44,524
How did you think of making pizza?

208
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:46,108
I was going to make kimchi <i>jjim.</i>

209
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:48,319
- But then I thought it'd be boring.
- Okay.

210
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:50,947
So I made pizza
with kimchi <i>jjim</i> ingredients as toppings.

211
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:53,616
- It's good.
- You like it?

212
00:08:53,699 --> 00:08:55,201
It tastes like real pizza.

213
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:56,869
Hold on.

214
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:01,082
Why is so much of mine left?

215
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:03,876
THE BOSS'S PIZZA

216
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:07,171
Maybe they liked
the milder one more than yours.

217
00:09:07,255 --> 00:09:08,798
Hey, this is bad.

218
00:09:09,507 --> 00:09:10,800
What happened?

219
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:18,516
- You can't eat spicy food?
- No.

220
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:20,017
It's spicy. Too spicy.

221
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:25,481
- It's spicy because of the peppers.
- Yes.

222
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:27,191
FLICKING OFF CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPERS

223
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:32,572
JUN-HO'S PIZZA

224
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:35,283
Cheongyang chili pepper. A bunch of it.

225
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:37,243
I guess they don't like the spicy one.

226
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:40,955
This one. Just a slice.

227
00:09:41,038 --> 00:09:42,498
Try it.

228
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:44,625
But it's quite spicy.

229
00:09:44,709 --> 00:09:46,210
He's terrible with spicy food.

230
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:47,753
ATTEMPT FAILS

231
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:48,754
It's okay.

232
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:50,923
- Even the mild one is spicy for him.
- The mild one?

233
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:52,425
Even the mild one's spicy?

234
00:09:52,508 --> 00:09:54,844
The kimchi is a bit spicy.

235
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:56,053
EVEN KIMCHI IS SPICY FOR HIM

236
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:57,805
- Because of the kimchi?
- He can't eat it.

237
00:09:59,557 --> 00:10:01,267
FEELING SOMEONE'S GAZE

238
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:02,893
You're eating Jun-ho's pizza too.

239
00:10:03,644 --> 00:10:05,271
I ate two of these.

240
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:06,939
- Two slices?
- Yes. It's good.

241
00:10:10,109 --> 00:10:12,820
When you made <i>okonomiyaki,</i>
did you feel like this too?

242
00:10:12,903 --> 00:10:15,489
- I thought, "Please finish all of it."
- Right?

243
00:10:15,573 --> 00:10:17,575
To see so much of it left,

244
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:19,327
it's weighing on me so much.

245
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,536
Oh, no.

246
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:22,538
I better eat all of the leftovers.

247
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:23,956
KIAN'S B&B

248
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,666
Shall we do the dishes?

249
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:27,752
IN CHARGE OF DISHWASHING
YEON-KOUNG AND ZUHA

250
00:10:27,835 --> 00:10:29,754
Is it more comfortable
to talk in Japanese?

251
00:10:31,255 --> 00:10:32,590
- Yes.
- Right?

252
00:10:32,673 --> 00:10:34,508
- It is a bit better, right?
- Yes.

253
00:10:34,592 --> 00:10:35,885
Is it tough, Kazuha?

254
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:37,470
Sorry?

255
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:39,764
Is it tough?

256
00:10:39,847 --> 00:10:41,098
No.

257
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:42,350
It's not?

258
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:44,101
I'm good.

259
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,645
You're good?

260
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:46,729
Yes.

261
00:10:47,813 --> 00:10:49,190
Want to do these by yourself?

262
00:10:49,273 --> 00:10:50,775
- It's tough.
- What?

263
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:51,817
It's really tough.

264
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:54,737
Do you have things to do?

265
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:56,739
- There's a lot to do.
