00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:31,409
And he's also studying
to become a teacher.

531
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:35,205
But even if two people
went through similar experiences,

532
00:23:35,288 --> 00:23:38,125
forming a close relationship like this
is not an easy thing.

533
00:23:38,208 --> 00:23:39,042
Right.

534
00:23:39,126 --> 00:23:41,586
You two must be on the same wavelength.

535
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:45,298
It must feel like
watching yourself when you were young.

536
00:23:45,382 --> 00:23:46,550
Totally.

537
00:23:46,633 --> 00:23:49,427
- You can relate to him.
- Yes.

538
00:23:49,511 --> 00:23:51,054
I've walked the same path.

539
00:23:53,014 --> 00:23:55,517
To me, the saddest thing is

540
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:57,310
he grew up too fast.

541
00:23:58,228 --> 00:23:59,771
Kids should be able to act cute

542
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:02,190
and whine a bit sometimes at that age.

543
00:24:04,985 --> 00:24:06,236
What was hard for me was…

544
00:24:09,823 --> 00:24:13,285
I just wanted to be
the same as the other kids.

545
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:16,705
When you're young, you want to fit in.

546
00:24:16,788 --> 00:24:17,831
Right.

547
00:24:17,914 --> 00:24:19,791
I didn't want anyone to know about it,

548
00:24:19,875 --> 00:24:22,169
so I think I hid it
and held myself back a lot.

549
00:24:22,252 --> 00:24:25,046
I realized not everyone was like me.

550
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:29,843
And when I realized my situation
wasn't actually a typical one,

551
00:24:30,468 --> 00:24:31,553
I thought,

552
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:35,015
"They said it was natural
to have parents."

553
00:24:35,098 --> 00:24:37,392
"If so, I should have parents too."

554
00:24:37,475 --> 00:24:40,520
"Then, where are mine?"

555
00:24:40,604 --> 00:24:43,273
So I thought,
"If I'm not even loved by my parents,

556
00:24:45,025 --> 00:24:47,777
what on earth am I?"

557
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:49,988
"Do I deserve to be loved?"

558
00:24:50,071 --> 00:24:52,115
I used to be obsessed with that thought.

559
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:55,243
I think that's why I couldn't love myself

560
00:24:55,327 --> 00:24:56,786
when I was young.

561
00:24:58,914 --> 00:25:02,125
And as a former teacher,
he's actively working

562
00:25:02,209 --> 00:25:06,338
on improving public awareness
of youths transitioning out of care.

563
00:25:06,922 --> 00:25:07,756
So…

564
00:25:08,340 --> 00:25:11,885
I want to do that too,
and that's how I want to live.

565
00:25:11,968 --> 00:25:16,348
I want to strive to achieve
such dreams as a teacher.

566
00:25:16,431 --> 00:25:17,891
He's your role model.

567
00:25:17,974 --> 00:25:19,392
You're right.

568
00:25:19,476 --> 00:25:22,687
