922
00:42:21,455 --> 00:42:25,167
You treated me like a friend
who came to hang out at your place.

923
00:42:25,251 --> 00:42:27,086
You made me feel like your brother

924
00:42:27,169 --> 00:42:28,921
or your friend.

925
00:42:29,004 --> 00:42:30,047
I had a blast.

926
00:42:30,631 --> 00:42:32,007
And I got to eat with the staff.

927
00:42:32,091 --> 00:42:34,093
That was what Boss wanted.

928
00:42:34,176 --> 00:42:36,053
Like you were visiting a friend's place.

929
00:42:36,136 --> 00:42:39,682
And so, when Smita and all of us
danced together then,

930
00:42:39,765 --> 00:42:40,683
it became a reality.

931
00:42:45,854 --> 00:42:47,439
<i>It was like we were very close friends.</i>

932
00:42:47,523 --> 00:42:50,317
<i>While all of us talked</i>
<i>and had fun together,</i>

933
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:51,360
<i>we became best friends.</i>

934
00:42:51,443 --> 00:42:54,321
<i>- Happy Birthday, dear Jun-ho</i>
<i>- Happy Birthday, dear Jun-ho</i>

935
00:42:54,405 --> 00:42:56,031
<i>I became best friends with a priest too.</i>

936
00:42:56,574 --> 00:42:58,284
I made many good friends here.

937
00:42:58,367 --> 00:42:59,243
- Right.
- For sure.

938
00:43:00,744 --> 00:43:02,538
- I'm glad to hear that.
- Right?

939
00:43:03,414 --> 00:43:07,084
DHARMA TEACHER HYEONUNG, LEE JUN-HO
IT WAS SHORT BUT WE MADE DEEP CONNECTIONS

940
00:43:07,710 --> 00:43:10,087
Mr. Kian, there's something
I wanted to give you.

941
00:43:10,170 --> 00:43:13,424
This is a singing bowl
I've used for a long time.

942
00:43:13,507 --> 00:43:14,758
- Isn't it precious to you?
- Yes.

943
00:43:14,842 --> 00:43:16,635
WATER OFFERING BOWL
SINGING BOWL

944
00:43:16,719 --> 00:43:18,345
- Thank you so much.
- Sure.

945
00:43:19,930 --> 00:43:21,849
Always think carefully.

946
00:43:21,932 --> 00:43:24,518
And whenever you feel stuck,
give it a hit.

947
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:26,186
I've only been taking things from you.

948
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:28,564
- No, not at all.
- And you're my guest.

949
00:43:29,189 --> 00:43:30,274
I had a great time.

950
00:43:30,357 --> 00:43:31,358
Thank you very much.

951
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:33,611
GAINS ANOTHER CHERISHED POSSESSION

952
00:43:33,694 --> 00:43:34,612
Checking out?

953
00:43:35,362 --> 00:43:38,449
I wish you all good health and peace.

954
00:43:38,532 --> 00:43:40,409
- I'll see you again one day.
- Sure.

955
00:43:40,492 --> 00:43:41,910
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

956
00:43:42,828 --> 00:43:44,330
I'll get going then.

957
00:43:44,413 --> 00:43:45,539
- Take care.
- Bye.

958
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:46,498
- Bye.
- Bye.

959
00:43:46,582 --> 00:43:48,042
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

960
00:43:49,251 --> 00:43:50,794
- Good luck!
- Good luck!

961
00:43:50,878 --> 00:43:52,880
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

962
00:43:56,759 --> 00:43:59,261
<i>Kian's B&B is "pollock."</i>

963
00:43:59,887 --> 00:44:02,264
<i>You see,</i>
<i>nothing goes to waste with pollock.</i>

964
00:44:02,348 --> 00:44:03,891
<i>Kian's B&B is just like that.</i>

965
00:44:05,934 --> 00:44:07,144
The weather's so nice.

966
00:44:07,227 --> 00:44:09,647
GUEST JUN-HO CHECKS OUT

967
00:44:09,730 --> 00:44:11,231
Gosh, he's gone.

968
00:44:12,274 --> 00:44:14,068
We should dust off this giant comforter.

969
00:44:14,151 --> 00:44:15,986
Let's do that then.

970
00:44:16,654 --> 00:44:18,113
All right. This is so big though.

971
00:44:18,197 --> 00:44:19,907
Hey, how do we…

972
00:44:19,990 --> 00:44:21,533
It's way too big.

973
00:44:21,617 --> 00:44:23,619
Let's each pull it back further.

974
00:44:23,702 --> 00:44:25,579
We should bunch up the edges a bit.

975
00:44:25,663 --> 00:44:27,289
- Or it'll drag on the ground.
- Right.

976
00:44:27,373 --> 00:44:28,248
Okay.

977
00:44:28,332 --> 00:44:29,416
Got it, right?

978
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:30,751
Hold onto the middle, everyone.

979
00:44:30,834 --> 00:44:32,294
We have to hold on like this.

980
00:44:32,378 --> 00:44:33,629
Hold on with two hands.

981
00:44:33,712 --> 00:44:34,963
Don't let it drag from here.

982
00:44:35,047 --> 00:44:36,006
CAREFUL

983
00:44:36,090 --> 00:44:36,924
Hold it high.

984
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:39,510
This is all about teamwork. Focus!

985
00:44:39,593 --> 00:44:40,594
Pull.

986
00:44:40,678 --> 00:44:42,262
Don't let it touch the ground.

987
00:44:42,346 --> 00:44:44,181
- Come this way.
- Hey, be careful.

988
00:44:44,264 --> 00:44:46,517
It's muddy over there.
Come here. Pull this way.

989
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:47,893
- Careful.
- Yeah, right there.

990
00:44:47,976 --> 00:44:49,937
- Kian, you'll slip.
- Don't get close.

991
00:44:50,020 --> 00:44:52,189
Okay, we'll shake it
up and down ten times.

992
00:44:52,272 --> 00:44:53,524
Ready, set, go.

993
00:44:54,441 --> 00:44:55,776
- One.
- Two.

994
00:44:55,859 --> 00:44:57,319
SHAKING COMFORTER ALONG TO THE COUNT

995
00:44:57,403 --> 00:45:00,114
Five, six, seven, eight.

996
00:45:00,197 --> 00:45:01,073
WHY IS IT FLAPPING?

997
00:45:01,156 --> 00:45:01,990
Pull!

998
00:45:03,492 --> 00:45:04,368
Spread out.

999
00:45:05,077 --> 00:45:08,414
THE ONLY ONE JUMPING UP AND DOWN

1000
00:45:08,497 --> 00:45:10,249
- Six, seven.
- Spread out.

1001
00:45:10,332 --> 00:45:12,292
Eight, nine, ten.

1002
00:45:12,876 --> 00:45:14,420
Hold on. Let's take a break.

1003
00:45:14,503 --> 00:45:15,712
Gosh, the dust.

1004
00:45:17,756 --> 00:45:19,049
BLOCKING THE DUST OUT

1005
00:45:19,133 --> 00:45:21,176
I think the dust
is collecting in the center.

1006
00:45:21,260 --> 00:45:23,262
- Exactly.
- Jun-ho, hold it like this with one hand.

1007
00:45:23,345 --> 00:45:25,097
- Boss, hold it like this.
- What?

1008
00:45:25,180 --> 00:45:26,014
Look.

1009
00:45:26,807 --> 00:45:29,143
Hold the middle like this
so it doesn't sag.

1010
00:45:29,226 --> 00:45:30,978
- Here we go.
- Ready, set, go.

1011
00:45:31,061 --> 00:45:32,563
ONE MORE TIME

1012
00:45:33,647 --> 00:45:36,400
JUMPS AROUND AGAIN AFTER CHANGING STANCE

1013
00:45:36,483 --> 00:45:38,569
Boss isn't doing it right.

1014
00:45:38,652 --> 00:45:40,237
Five, six…

1015
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:42,990
Eight, nine…

1016
00:45:44,491 --> 00:45:46,410
Why are you flapping around so much?

1017
00:45:46,493 --> 00:45:48,871
Shake along to the count!

1018
00:45:48,954 --> 00:45:50,998
But you didn't count!

1019
00:45:51,081 --> 00:45:52,124
God, this is tiring.

1020
00:45:52,207 --> 00:45:55,169
Why are you ignoring the count
and flapping around on your own?

1021
00:45:55,752 --> 00:45:57,796
You looked like a fairy

1022
00:45:57,880 --> 00:45:59,131
who was about to fly away.

1023
00:45:59,214 --> 00:46:01,633
- She said you looked like a fairy.
- A fairy? I did?

1024
00:46:01,717 --> 00:46:03,010
Fairies are cute.

1025
00:46:04,386 --> 00:46:05,512
Now, let's fold it up.

1026
00:46:05,596 --> 00:46:07,347
This way? Like this?

1027
00:46:08,515 --> 00:46:10,517
- Pull both ends there.
- That's right.

1028
00:46:10,601 --> 00:46:11,810
Meet in the middle.

1029
00:46:12,478 --> 00:46:15,522
Now go back,
and let's meet in the middle again.

1030
00:46:15,606 --> 00:46:16,690
In the middle.

1031
00:46:16,773 --> 00:46:17,983
We've folded it so many times.

1032
00:46:18,066 --> 00:46:19,860
Could there be
a bigger comforter in Korea?

1033
00:46:19,943 --> 00:46:21,528
- No way.
- We have to put it away.

1034
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:23,030
One, two, three.

1035
00:46:24,156 --> 00:46:25,115
All done.

1036
00:46:25,824 --> 00:46:28,619
THEY DISPERSE AND START CLEANING

1037
00:46:30,746 --> 00:46:32,206
EVERY CORNER

1038
00:46:32,289 --> 00:46:34,374
Gosh, it's so dusty here.

1039
00:46:36,752 --> 00:46:38,504
It's so dirty today.

1040
00:46:42,007 --> 00:46:43,050
Goodness.

1041
00:46:43,133 --> 00:46:44,968
Gosh, I keep saying "goodness."

1042
00:46:45,552 --> 00:46:48,138
It really is dirty.
There's so much to clean.

1043
00:46:49,765 --> 00:46:51,058
Zuha's doing well.

1044
00:46:51,141 --> 00:46:52,100
She works hard.

1045
00:46:55,395 --> 00:46:56,897
We're just cleaning all day.

1046
00:46:58,440 --> 00:46:59,858
We're cleaning properly today.

1047
00:47:01,318 --> 00:47:02,569
I think we're pretty much done.

1048
00:47:03,153 --> 00:47:04,112
It looks clean.

1049
00:47:05,322 --> 00:47:06,740
ALPENSIA SKI JUMPING CENTER

1050
00:47:06,823 --> 00:47:08,534
GI-PYO, JIN-AN, YOUNG-HYUN

1051
00:47:09,243 --> 00:47:10,619
Man, it's huge.

1052
00:47:10,702 --> 00:47:11,995
ALPENSIA SKI JUMPING CENTER

1053
00:47:14,957 --> 00:47:17,042
ABOUT A 93-M-TALL
SKI JUMP TOWER

1054
00:47:17,125 --> 00:47:19,294
I can't believe we're sledding here.

1055
00:47:19,378 --> 00:47:20,462
I never imagined it.

1056
00:47:21,129 --> 00:47:23,590
SLEDDING ON A SKI JUMP RAMP

1057
00:47:28,470 --> 00:47:30,806
The slope feels different this way.

1058
00:47:32,432 --> 00:47:33,684
<i>Where did Taro go?</i>

1059
00:47:33,767 --> 00:47:35,310
SONGJEONGHAEBYEON BEACH

1060
00:47:35,394 --> 00:47:36,687
KOTARO, YOO-MIN

1061
00:47:36,770 --> 00:47:38,855
It's the sea!

1062
00:47:38,939 --> 00:47:40,941
Gosh, this is so moving.

1063
00:47:41,024 --> 00:47:42,401
SONGJEONGHAEBYEON BEACH

1064
00:47:42,484 --> 00:47:43,819
It's so pretty.

1065
00:47:43,902 --> 00:47:45,612
Yoo-min, be careful!

1066
00:47:47,739 --> 00:47:52,786
Let's see who can find the cuter shell.

1067
00:47:52,869 --> 00:47:54,204
Two shells?

1068
00:47:54,288 --> 00:47:56,373
Okay. Decision time!

1069
00:47:56,456 --> 00:47:57,916
One, two!

1070
00:47:58,000 --> 00:47:59,418
Ta-da!

1071
00:47:59,501 --> 00:48:01,169
Taro.

1072
00:48:02,546 --> 00:48:04,756
<i>What a cool picture!</i>

1073
00:48:04,840 --> 00:48:06,967
<i>You look so pretty.</i>

1074
00:48:07,050 --> 00:48:09,303
<i>This is so nice.</i>

1075
00:48:13,724 --> 00:48:15,183
BONGPYEONG

1076
00:48:15,267 --> 00:48:17,519
SUNG-NAM, SEONG-JUN

1077
00:48:17,603 --> 00:48:18,812
- It's the memorial hall?
- Yeah.

1078
00:48:18,895 --> 00:48:19,896
LEE HYOSEOK MEMORIAL HALL

1079
00:48:20,522 --> 00:48:22,316
"When Buckwheat Flowers Bloom."

1080
00:48:22,899 --> 00:48:24,234
Did you read this in school too?

1081
00:48:24,318 --> 00:48:26,028
- This short story?
- Of course.

1082
00:48:26,111 --> 00:48:29,239
Where did he get such inspiration from?

1083
00:48:29,323 --> 00:48:30,741
LEE HYOSEOK'S BIRTHPLACE

1084
00:48:30,824 --> 00:48:32,242
They'd make these back in the day.

1085
00:48:32,326 --> 00:48:34,786
NATIONAL MUSEUM
OF THE ANNALS OF THE JOSEON DYNASTY

1086
00:48:34,870 --> 00:48:36,371
A TOUR FULL OF PASSION FOR LEARNING

1087
00:48:36,455 --> 00:48:38,165
It was returned after 100 years.

1088
00:48:39,708 --> 00:48:41,376
It was built in 1606?

1089
00:48:42,002 --> 00:48:43,337
<i>"Bangsangsi."</i>

1090
00:48:44,755 --> 00:48:46,590
- We're checking out tomorrow.
- Right.

1091
00:48:46,673 --> 00:48:47,758
It feels so short.

1092
00:48:47,841 --> 00:48:49,009
What a shame.

1093
00:48:50,302 --> 00:48:52,179
AT LAST DESTINATION
WITH BITTERSWEET FEELINGS

1094
00:48:52,262 --> 00:48:53,096
Family photos.

1095
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:55,182
- Hello.
- Hello.

1096
00:48:55,265 --> 00:48:56,850
- We'd like to take a photo.
- Sure.

1097
00:48:59,853 --> 00:49:01,396
- Like this?
- Like this?

1098
00:49:03,899 --> 00:49:05,359
My skin looks fairer too.

1099
00:49:05,442 --> 00:49:07,486
It looks good. It came out well.

1100
00:49:08,236 --> 00:49:10,072
I've wanted to do this since 10th grade.

1101
00:49:10,155 --> 00:49:11,281
- I see.
- Yes.

1102
00:49:11,365 --> 00:49:14,660
I must be getting old. I'm tearing up.

1103
00:49:14,743 --> 00:49:16,953
2:00 P.M.

1104
00:49:17,037 --> 00:49:18,622
What's that? Did you write down plans?

1105
00:49:18,705 --> 00:49:21,875
There are just a few days left.
I'm going to plan them like this.

1106
00:49:21,958 --> 00:49:23,377
That's cool.

1107
00:49:23,460 --> 00:49:25,295
How many nights are there?
One, two, three.

1108
00:49:25,379 --> 00:49:27,089
- Four nights.
- There are four nights left.

1109
00:49:27,172 --> 00:49:29,466
It can be about the plan, new ideas,

1110
00:49:29,549 --> 00:49:31,385
or anything you want to change.

1111
00:49:31,468 --> 00:49:33,303
Any opinions?

1112
00:49:33,387 --> 00:49:34,388
- First, for today…
- Yes?

1113
00:49:34,471 --> 00:49:35,555
I have to go to the market.

1114
00:49:35,639 --> 00:49:36,682
YEON-KOUNG IS TODAY'S CHEF

1115
00:49:36,765 --> 00:49:37,933
You're making pasta, right?

1116
00:49:38,016 --> 00:49:41,353
Pasta and chicken breast <i>naengchae</i> salad?

1117
00:49:41,436 --> 00:49:43,689
I'll help you when you cook.

1118
00:49:43,772 --> 00:49:45,357
About the karaoke room,

1119
00:49:45,440 --> 00:49:49,569
I think it's better to open it
the night before someone checks out.

1120
00:49:50,153 --> 00:49:52,239
Tonight's the last night
for three of them.

1121
00:49:52,322 --> 00:49:53,824
And the other four.

1122
00:49:54,449 --> 00:49:55,784
- They all leave.
- What?

1123
00:49:55,867 --> 00:49:57,202
They all leave tomorrow.

1124
00:49:58,370 --> 00:50:00,122
ALL OF THE GUESTS CHECK OUT TOMORROW

1125
00:50:00,205 --> 00:50:01,456
- Right.
- Three-day stays.

1126
00:50:01,540 --> 00:50:03,500
THE KARAOKE ROOM WILL OPEN TONIGHT

1127
00:50:03,583 --> 00:50:05,001
- But I think…
- Yeah?

1128
00:50:05,627 --> 00:50:06,920
It feels like

1129
00:50:07,003 --> 00:50:08,505
we always have dinner.

1130
00:50:08,588 --> 00:50:10,424
Then, we either wash up or use the sauna.

1131
00:50:10,507 --> 00:50:14,344
And then, we have a drink,
and that's how it usually goes.

1132
00:50:14,428 --> 00:50:18,306
I do think it'd be nice to let them
drink during dinner if they want.

1133
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:21,727
You know what, Yeon-koung?
How about we give that a try today?

1134
00:50:21,810 --> 00:50:23,145
GIVE WHAT A TRY?

1135
00:50:23,228 --> 00:50:25,397
- Serve everything like a buffet.
- Okay.

1136
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:26,982
And let them on their own…

1137
00:50:27,065 --> 00:50:28,942
Including beverages and alcohol?

1138
00:50:29,025 --> 00:50:30,193
Yeah, and let them eat

1139
00:50:30,277 --> 00:50:32,028
like a wedding buffet.

1140
00:50:32,112 --> 00:50:34,030
- They can drink too.
- That's not a bad idea.

1141
00:50:34,114 --> 00:50:35,741
- Like a party?
- Yeah.

1142
00:50:35,824 --> 00:50:39,077
You know, like going around
drinking and mingling.

1143
00:50:39,161 --> 00:50:40,662
We'll make it feel like a party.

1144
00:50:40,746 --> 00:50:42,789
Right, it has to feel like a party.

1145
00:50:42,873 --> 00:50:43,999
What should we call it?

1146
00:50:44,082 --> 00:50:45,959
- "Happy Kian's B&B Day"?
- That's good.

1147
00:50:47,085 --> 00:50:49,087
But what do you do at a party?

1148
00:50:49,171 --> 00:50:51,089
- Like usually?
- You usually dress up.

1149
00:50:51,173 --> 00:50:53,008
As if you're the most stylish person ever.

1150
00:50:53,091 --> 00:50:53,925
Right.

1151
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:55,927
Get dressed up for tonight then.

1152
00:50:56,011 --> 00:50:57,429
You have to dress up too.

1153
00:50:57,512 --> 00:50:59,014
- Me?
- You can finally wear that suit.

1154
00:50:59,097 --> 00:51:01,266
I thought I'd never be able to
wear it again here.

1155
00:51:01,349 --> 00:51:02,768
- Finally.
- You have to wear it.

1156
00:51:02,851 --> 00:51:04,019
That's some good news.

1157
00:51:04,102 --> 00:51:06,271
But will there be enough time?

1158
00:51:06,354 --> 00:51:07,481
- It'll be tight.
- Right?

1159
00:51:07,564 --> 00:51:10,650
Or while we cook, you and Zuha can…

1160
00:51:10,734 --> 00:51:12,736
- Set up?
- We could do it then.

1161
00:51:12,819 --> 00:51:14,237
Spruce the place up.

1162
00:51:14,321 --> 00:51:15,906
- Good idea, right?
- Yeah.

1163
00:51:15,989 --> 00:51:17,741
I guess this is why we need meetings.

1164
00:51:17,824 --> 00:51:19,242
SATISFIED

1165
00:51:19,326 --> 00:51:20,786
Let's go out and buy groceries.

1166
00:51:20,869 --> 00:51:22,078
Okay, let's go.

1167
00:51:22,704 --> 00:51:23,830
Let's buy them quickly.

1168
00:51:24,581 --> 00:51:26,041
We have to buy beer and soju.

1169
00:51:26,792 --> 00:51:28,543
CANNED DRINKS FOR THE PARTY

1170
00:51:28,627 --> 00:51:30,170
Cans.

1171
00:51:30,253 --> 00:51:32,881
We'll take that cake. Yes, thank you.

1172
00:51:33,507 --> 00:51:35,550
- We're here.
- Let's go.

1173
00:51:35,634 --> 00:51:37,135
- Here we go.
- All right.

1174
00:51:37,219 --> 00:51:38,136
HURRYING BACK HOME

1175
00:51:38,220 --> 00:51:39,763
We picked a good cake.

1176
00:51:39,846 --> 00:51:42,140
- It gives off party vibes.
- Right.

1177
00:51:44,226 --> 00:51:46,061
DEALING WITH THE DOOR FOR THE FIFTH DAY

1178
00:51:46,144 --> 00:51:46,978
I'm so tired.

1179
00:51:50,232 --> 00:51:52,025
- Why won't it open?
- It's open.

1180
00:51:52,108 --> 00:51:53,235
It's open.

1181
00:51:54,694 --> 00:51:55,612
Go in.

1182
00:51:55,695 --> 00:51:56,780
I had no energy to jump.

1183
00:51:56,863 --> 00:51:58,073
Isn't it so funny?

1184
00:52:02,536 --> 00:52:04,996
- About time you got a call, right?
- Right.

1185
00:52:05,080 --> 00:52:05,914
3:30 P.M.

1186
00:52:07,123 --> 00:52:08,583
I guess no one's checking in today.

1187
00:52:09,167 --> 00:52:10,544
- We're not getting any calls.
- No.

1188
00:52:10,627 --> 00:52:11,837
WITHOUT NEW GUESTS CHECKING IN

1189
00:52:12,671 --> 00:52:14,506
THEY START PREPPING FOR THE PARTY

1190
00:52:14,589 --> 00:52:16,591
- We have to cook, right?
- Yes.

1191
00:52:16,675 --> 00:52:17,968
I'll assist you.

1192
00:52:18,051 --> 00:52:21,096
TODAY'S SOUS-CHEF AND MAIN CHEF

1193
00:52:21,680 --> 00:52:22,889
What will you do first?

1194
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:26,643
I'm going to boil chicken first.
It takes the longest.

1195
00:52:26,726 --> 00:52:28,436
Put all the chicken in at once?

1196
00:52:29,145 --> 00:52:31,398
- You know the amount. I don't know.
- Just put them in?

1197
00:52:31,481 --> 00:52:32,983
CHICKEN BREAST FOR SALAD

1198
00:52:33,066 --> 00:52:35,110
There are 11 people.

1199
00:52:35,193 --> 00:52:37,195
- So this much for now?
- Sure.

1200
00:52:38,738 --> 00:52:41,032
IN CHARGE OF DECORATION

1201
00:52:41,116 --> 00:52:42,284
Hey, just put the beer…

1202
00:52:42,367 --> 00:52:44,411
Here? Or outside to chill them?

1203
00:52:44,494 --> 00:52:45,912
- Let's just put them outside.
- Okay.

1204
00:52:45,996 --> 00:52:47,038
Okay.

1205
00:52:47,873 --> 00:52:49,332
- All done.
- That's it.

1206
00:52:49,416 --> 00:52:50,584
You can go back in, Zuha.

1207
00:52:50,667 --> 00:52:51,751
DRINKS PUT OUTSIDE TO CHILL

1208
00:52:51,835 --> 00:52:53,003
I'll do it.

1209
00:52:53,920 --> 00:52:55,130
- Boss.
- Yeah?

1210
00:52:55,213 --> 00:52:56,965
We're getting rid of this, right?

1211
00:52:57,048 --> 00:52:59,175
- What?
- The mat here.

1212
00:52:59,259 --> 00:53:00,927
- We have to fold it up.
- Fold it?

1213
00:53:01,011 --> 00:53:02,929
- You're going to do it alone?
- I don't know.

1214
00:53:03,513 --> 00:53:04,764
It won't be easy.

1215
00:53:08,393 --> 00:53:11,605
1ST PREPARATION FOR HAPPY KIAN'S B&B DAY
FOLD THE MAT

1216
00:53:11,688 --> 00:53:14,524
THE MAT THAT ZUHA WILL FOLD BY HERSELF IS…

1217
00:53:16,359 --> 00:53:19,404
ABOUT AS BIG AS 44 ZUHAS

1218
00:53:21,948 --> 00:53:24,326
AND WEIGHS ABOUT 200 KG

1219
00:53:29,080 --> 00:53:29,915
FOLDS THE CORNER

1220
00:53:29,998 --> 00:53:30,916
Lift it here.

1221
00:53:30,999 --> 00:53:32,292
And fold this.

1222
00:53:35,545 --> 00:53:36,546
LET'S GO BACK

1223
00:53:40,216 --> 00:53:42,093
IT'S NOT EASY

1224
00:53:44,429 --> 00:53:46,222
5 MINUTES SPENT ON ONE SIDE

1225
00:53:46,306 --> 00:53:47,223
Are you okay?

1226
00:53:51,645 --> 00:53:53,980
THE MAT CAN'T BE PULLED

1227
00:53:56,232 --> 00:53:58,818
IT PUSHES ZUHA BACK

1228
00:54:05,533 --> 00:54:06,910
- You're doing well.
- Right?

1229
00:54:06,993 --> 00:54:08,161
AND THE ONE LAUGHING

1230
00:54:08,244 --> 00:54:10,372
- Fold it.
- But am I doing it right?

1231
00:54:10,455 --> 00:54:12,248
- Does it fold in half?
- You figure it out.

1232
00:54:13,667 --> 00:54:15,752
ANNOYED

1233
00:54:15,835 --> 00:54:18,213
Just pull and fold it up.

1234
00:54:18,296 --> 00:54:19,297
You're doing well.

1235
00:54:19,381 --> 00:54:20,340
GLARING

1236
00:54:20,423 --> 00:54:24,386
You say it like it's easy,
but it's so hard.

1237
00:54:27,889 --> 00:54:29,474
It's unfolding over there.

1238
00:54:36,648 --> 00:54:38,650
I can't do this.

1239
00:54:39,317 --> 00:54:41,152
How am I supposed to do this by myself?

1240
00:54:42,237 --> 00:54:43,363
<i>I mean, from upstairs,</i>

1241
00:54:43,446 --> 00:54:44,739
standing like this,

1242
00:54:44,823 --> 00:54:46,866
he said, "You figure it out."

1243
00:54:46,950 --> 00:54:48,660
I guess it's that kind of place.

1244
00:54:49,327 --> 00:54:50,996
You have to handle things by yourself.

1245
00:54:51,079 --> 00:54:52,706
KIAN'S PHILOSOPHY
HANDLE IT YOURSELF

1246
00:54:53,999 --> 00:54:56,292
FIGURING OUT BY HERSELF

1247
00:54:56,376 --> 00:54:57,752
This is crazy.

1248
00:55:03,008 --> 00:55:05,552
SHE SEES KIAN FROM BEHIND

1249
00:55:10,682 --> 00:55:11,641
What was that?

1250
00:55:13,018 --> 00:55:14,728
SENSING MURDEROUS INTENT

1251
00:55:16,771 --> 00:55:18,106
Sorry? What?

1252
00:55:18,189 --> 00:55:19,065
PLAYING DUMB

1253
00:55:20,358 --> 00:55:24,279
WHILE AT LEAST HALF AS BEEN FOLDED

1254
00:55:25,530 --> 00:55:28,158
HE STRUGGLES TO FIND SUPPLIES

1255
00:55:28,241 --> 00:55:29,492
Why is it so bare-bones?

1256
00:55:32,787 --> 00:55:35,707
AFTER INVENTORY CHECK,
HE RETURNS EMPTY-HANDED

1257
00:55:36,875 --> 00:55:39,335
Zuha, you were doing it alone? I'm sorry.

1258
00:55:39,419 --> 00:55:41,671
- Why weren't you helping?
- Sorry.

1259
00:55:41,755 --> 00:55:43,548
I thought you were bringing in a table.

1260
00:55:43,631 --> 00:55:45,467
I looked for it, but there was no table.

1261
00:55:45,550 --> 00:55:46,509
- Really?
- Here.

1262
00:55:46,593 --> 00:55:47,969
One, two, three.

1263
00:55:50,472 --> 00:55:52,348
Geez, what is up with this?

1264
00:55:52,932 --> 00:55:56,061
This may be several hundred kilograms.
How did you do this by yourself?

1265
00:55:56,144 --> 00:55:58,688
Gosh, many things happened.

1266
00:55:59,689 --> 00:56:01,107
One, two, three.

1267
00:56:02,942 --> 00:56:04,444
- Is this right?
- It is.

1268
00:56:04,527 --> 00:56:05,695
AFTER STRUGGLES, SHE FOLDS IT

1269
00:56:05,779 --> 00:56:08,239
Maybe we should just push it to that side.

1270
00:56:08,323 --> 00:56:09,240
- Really?
- Yeah.

1271
00:56:11,201 --> 00:56:12,452
Yes.

1272
00:56:12,535 --> 00:56:13,787
- Pull the bottom.
- Wait.

1273
00:56:13,870 --> 00:56:14,829
Yes, right there.

1274
00:56:19,292 --> 00:56:20,710
She took off her socks.

1275
00:56:21,252 --> 00:56:23,755
Yeah, I'll pull and you push.
One, two, three.

1276
00:56:23,838 --> 00:56:25,924
PUSHES ON IN BARE FEET

1277
00:56:26,007 --> 00:56:27,050
Now, the other side.

1278
00:56:27,592 --> 00:56:29,677
Isn't the floor all burned though?

1279
00:56:29,761 --> 00:56:30,720
It is.

1280
00:56:30,804 --> 00:56:33,556
WELL-COOKED FLOOR

1281
00:56:33,640 --> 00:56:37,227
Every house in the countryside
used to have floors like this. It's okay.

1282
00:56:37,310 --> 00:56:39,979
- They look like a loaves of bread.
- You're right.

1283
00:56:40,063 --> 00:56:41,272
They are loaves of bread.

1284
00:56:41,356 --> 00:56:42,440
All right. That will do.

1285
00:56:42,524 --> 00:56:44,067
PARTY SPACE SECURED

1286
00:56:44,150 --> 00:56:46,236
- Your feet look cooked.
- Right?

1287
00:56:46,319 --> 00:56:47,362
BROWN AT THE WARMEST SPOTS

1288
00:56:47,445 --> 00:56:48,613
It's that hot.

1289
00:56:48,696 --> 00:56:51,908
No, if we open the window for a bit,

1290
00:56:51,991 --> 00:56:52,867
it'll be okay.

1291
00:56:52,951 --> 00:56:54,369
It's because we kept the mat on.

1292
00:56:54,452 --> 00:56:55,912
- That's why, right?
- Yeah.

1293
00:56:57,789 --> 00:56:59,124
- Geez.
- Look at this.

1294
00:56:59,207 --> 00:57:00,583
- The floor.
- It got a proper burn.

1295
00:57:00,667 --> 00:57:02,043
- It definitely did.
- Yeah.

1296
00:57:02,127 --> 00:57:03,795
- Is it okay?
- No wonder why it was so hot.

1297
00:57:03,878 --> 00:57:07,549
So how do you want to do it?
Like an awards show?

1298
00:57:07,632 --> 00:57:08,967
That'd be the best choice.

1299
00:57:09,050 --> 00:57:10,260
Make it like an awards show?

1300
00:57:10,343 --> 00:57:12,804
Yeah, like the Baeksang Arts Awards.

1301
00:57:12,887 --> 00:57:14,013
This is the stage then?

1302
00:57:14,097 --> 00:57:15,849
I think three tables would be perfect.

1303
00:57:15,932 --> 00:57:18,143
- Put tables here?
- Three tables.

1304
00:57:18,226 --> 00:57:21,563
There, there, and there.
And the stage would be up there.

1305
00:57:21,646 --> 00:57:23,523
And as they enjoy the party…

1306
00:57:23,606 --> 00:57:24,566
With chairs too?

1307
00:57:24,649 --> 00:57:26,943
We'll say,
"Everyone, we'll begin the party."

1308
00:57:27,026 --> 00:57:30,613
"Are you guys enjoying your last night?"
Something like that.

1309
00:57:30,697 --> 00:57:31,739
Okay, we'll give it a try.

1310
00:57:31,823 --> 00:57:33,032
LET'S DO IT AWARDS SHOW-STYLE

1311
00:57:33,616 --> 00:57:34,993
You know the tables outside?

1312
00:57:35,076 --> 00:57:36,619
Let's clean them and bring them in.

1313
00:57:36,703 --> 00:57:38,705
- In the outdoor tent?
- You know. Yeah.

1314
00:57:38,788 --> 00:57:39,622
Outside.

1315
00:57:39,706 --> 00:57:40,665
Okay.

1316
00:57:40,748 --> 00:57:42,750
2ND PREPARATION
GET TABLES AND CHAIRS

1317
00:57:43,418 --> 00:57:46,379
We're trying to turn
Boss's imagination into reality.

1318
00:57:47,505 --> 00:57:48,673
But it's so hard.

1319
00:57:49,507 --> 00:57:52,051
But to be honest,
you can't figure him out, can you?

1320
00:57:52,135 --> 00:57:53,386
CAN'T FOLLOW HIS THOUGHTS

1321
00:57:53,470 --> 00:57:55,847
I think he'll be satisfied
if there are tables.

1322
00:57:55,930 --> 00:57:57,098
I think so too.

1323
00:57:57,182 --> 00:57:59,017
Let's do it like the Baeksang Arts Awards.

1324
00:57:59,100 --> 00:58:00,768
TO MAKE HIS IMAGINATION A REALITY

1325
00:58:00,852 --> 00:58:02,562
THEY SEARCH STORAGE FIRST

1326
00:58:02,645 --> 00:58:04,397
- Look at this.
- Are those the chairs?

1327
00:58:04,481 --> 00:58:06,483
But you think these will do?

1328
00:58:06,566 --> 00:58:07,567
CHAIRS THEY NEED TO TAKE

1329
00:58:07,650 --> 00:58:10,987
Then, let's bring the whole box and…

1330
00:58:11,070 --> 00:58:12,405
Use that as a table?

1331
00:58:12,489 --> 00:58:13,656
A BLUE BOX FOR A TABLE

1332
00:58:13,740 --> 00:58:15,492
I heard there are wine glasses here.

1333
00:58:15,575 --> 00:58:16,993
Here they are.

1334
00:58:17,076 --> 00:58:18,161
Let's bring them.

1335
00:58:18,244 --> 00:58:19,078
Let's go.

1336
00:58:20,371 --> 00:58:21,456
I'll put them here for now.

1337
00:58:21,539 --> 00:58:22,624
THEY RAID STORAGE FIRST

1338
00:58:23,291 --> 00:58:24,876
- Let's bring one table first.
- Okay.

1339
00:58:24,959 --> 00:58:26,711
- And all the chairs?
- Yes. We'll take this.

1340
00:58:26,794 --> 00:58:27,629
OUTDOOR TENT IS NEXT

1341
00:58:28,213 --> 00:58:29,422
Just like that.

1342
00:58:30,632 --> 00:58:33,343
THEY TAKE THE CAMPING TABLE AND CHAIRS TOO

1343
00:58:34,177 --> 00:58:35,637
- What on earth?
- What?

1344
00:58:35,720 --> 00:58:36,930
- Are there cows?
- Yeah, look.

1345
00:58:37,013 --> 00:58:38,056
THEY SEE COWS UPON RETURN

1346
00:58:39,390 --> 00:58:40,517
Gosh.

1347
00:58:40,600 --> 00:58:41,768
Are they milk cows?

1348
00:58:43,269 --> 00:58:44,521
BRIEF PAUSE TO WATCH COWS

1349
00:58:44,604 --> 00:58:45,897
That must be the mother cow.

1350
00:58:46,397 --> 00:58:49,317
I think it's the big black one.

1351
00:58:49,817 --> 00:58:51,194
She saw us.

1352
00:58:51,277 --> 00:58:52,695
- Our eyes met.
- Right.

1353
00:58:53,780 --> 00:58:54,739
Not scared?

1354
00:58:54,822 --> 00:58:56,074
- I think it's okay.
- Really?

1355
00:58:56,616 --> 00:58:58,535
- No, I meant you.
- Me? I'm fine.

1356
00:58:58,618 --> 00:58:59,536
I like animals.

1357
00:58:59,619 --> 00:59:00,662
- You do?
- Yes.

1358
00:59:01,287 --> 00:59:02,497
She's coming.

1359
00:59:02,580 --> 00:59:03,915
She's coming over here.

1360
00:59:04,707 --> 00:59:06,543
- Does she want to fight?
- Right?

1361
00:59:06,626 --> 00:59:07,919
- You should…
- Do something.

1362
00:59:08,002 --> 00:59:09,295
You stay back a bit.

1363
00:59:09,379 --> 00:59:10,630
I think I'll lose.

1364
00:59:11,714 --> 00:59:13,424
Which animal is your favorite?

1365
00:59:13,967 --> 00:59:15,260
- Dogs.
- Dogs?

1366
00:59:15,343 --> 00:59:16,678
She's very different from a dog.

1367
00:59:16,761 --> 00:59:18,763
A "DOG" AT KIAN'S B&B

1368
00:59:19,681 --> 00:59:20,515
HE CALLS HER

1369
00:59:20,598 --> 00:59:21,474
It's all right.

1370
00:59:22,141 --> 00:59:23,643
- Just once…
- Is it okay?

1371
00:59:23,726 --> 00:59:24,602
Be careful.

1372
00:59:27,021 --> 00:59:28,565
- Zuha, now's the time.
- Be careful.

1373
00:59:28,648 --> 00:59:29,524
Now's the time.

1374
00:59:30,733 --> 00:59:31,651
There you go.

1375
00:59:32,360 --> 00:59:33,236
Right now.

1376
00:59:33,987 --> 00:59:38,533
Wait! Hey, not this!

1377
00:59:38,616 --> 00:59:41,327
- No, they're glasses!
- It was so hard to find these!

1378
00:59:41,953 --> 00:59:43,788
If you hold this, she'll come to you.

1379
00:59:44,414 --> 00:59:45,540
- No!
- Bye.

1380
00:59:45,623 --> 00:59:47,584
- Sorry.
- Hey, watch out for poop.

1381
00:59:49,294 --> 00:59:52,463
- She's coming!
- Come on!

1382
00:59:52,547 --> 00:59:53,881
- It's because of this.
- Hurry up.

1383
00:59:53,965 --> 00:59:54,799
Let's hurry.

1384
00:59:54,882 --> 00:59:56,134
- She's coming.
- Hurry up.

1385
00:59:56,217 --> 00:59:57,677
No, we have to leave the box behind.

1386
00:59:57,760 --> 00:59:59,345
What are you talking about? Hurry up!

1387
00:59:59,846 --> 01:00:00,680
Run faster, Zuha.

1388
01:00:01,848 --> 01:00:04,225
- Geez, what are we doing?
- Gosh, there it is.

1389
01:00:05,393 --> 01:00:07,020
- Sorry!
- Bye.

1390
01:00:07,103 --> 01:00:08,229
HURRIEDLY SAYS GOODBYE

1391
01:00:11,816 --> 01:00:14,068
- You can just bring the chairs.
- Okay.

1392
01:00:14,944 --> 01:00:17,071
Will I be able to carry all of them?

1393
01:00:20,408 --> 01:00:21,492
Can you carry all of them?

1394
01:00:22,368 --> 01:00:26,414
STRONG ZUHA

1395
01:00:26,497 --> 01:00:27,915
Okay, good.

1396
01:00:27,999 --> 01:00:30,209
- It's better than making multiple trips.
- Right.

1397
01:00:31,586 --> 01:00:32,879
Nice, you're doing well.

1398
01:00:34,464 --> 01:00:35,465
Watch your step.

1399
01:00:35,548 --> 01:00:36,716
STUMBLES

1400
01:00:39,344 --> 01:00:40,511
What is it?

1401
01:00:41,638 --> 01:00:44,182
- What is it?
- Darn it, I stepped on poop!

1402
01:00:44,265 --> 01:00:45,683
I stepped on poop!

1403
01:00:45,767 --> 01:00:48,561
<i>You didn't just step on it.</i>
<i>You rubbed it in, Zuha.</i>

1404
01:00:48,645 --> 01:00:49,479
KIAN'S BIZARRE B&B SEASON 2

1405
01:01:35,233 --> 01:01:37,235
Subtitle translation by: Wayne Ryu
